Rewritten 2026-07-06 as an unordered backlog; completed work and its
rationale live in the git history of this file, docs/design/, and NEWS.

Items are listed alphabetically by plan name; the order carries no
meaning. Every item has an implementation plan in docs/plans/<name>.md,
and the planning/implementation/review process (who plans, who
implements, who reviews, which gates run) is docs/plans/README.md.
"window: pre-release" marks items whose cheap form expires when 1.0-0
freezes the R and dbarts.h compatibility contracts: they need a
go/no-go decision before submission, not necessarily the work itself.

Standing fact (VD, 2026-07-06): single-chain n >= 1e5 workloads are
common. The large-n performance items are live, not consumer-gated.

items
  blocked-jacobi-trees: exact parallel tree updates via noise-splitting
    augmentation (per-tree pseudo-responses y_k ~ N(g_k, sigma^2/b),
    sum-constrained): b trees update independently per barrier at the
    cost of b-fold precision on structure moves. Candidate mechanism
    for within-chain-threading; an ESS-per-second experiment decides.
  block-fusion: frontier-3.4 block-fused atom map, the flagship large-n
    engine lever (design docs/design/block-fusion.md; targets ~6x DRAM
    drop at n >= 1e5). STAGE A LANDED 2026-07-11 (bartcore d9a5d39,
    default-ON): the b=1 exact refactor - the constant-leaf steady-state
    sweep sources per-leaf sufficient statistics through the atom path
    (src/bartcore/atoms.hpp) and birth/death/change/swap are atom-routed,
    all bit-identical (equivalence 22/22, tinytest no-regen, bench
    neutral). Plan docs/plans/block-fusion-stage-a.md. STAGE B NEXT (the
    speed win): turn on b>1, regroup the suffstat/roll/draw to O(atoms),
    carries the single VD-approved one-time re-record; plan
    docs/plans/block-fusion-stage-b.md (to be written). Stage C: tune b.
    Scope v1 = constant-leaf Gaussian. Subsumes the standalone
    contiguous-layout item.
  data-ownership: own predictor storage instead of borrowing REAL(x)
    (drops the PROT_* pinning and the const_cast write-through);
    changes the documented aliasing of per-observation updates.
    window: pre-release. Review-6 notes: add COLUMN-SUBSET views
    (buildFromParent is row-subset only - hard prerequisite for BCF
    moderators and per-forest predictors); guardrail - the constant
    leaf's centered-SS and the BCF 1e-9 floor are numerically safe
    ONLY because responses arrive pre-standardized to O(1); the
    owned container must not create a path that feeds raw-scale
    residuals to the leaves.
  gpu-bart: memo + falsifiers landed (docs/design/gpu-bart.md,
    docs/design/parallel-bart-frontier.md). Backend-seam design still
    waits on frontier items 4-5 (informed-kernel + CG-leaf prototypes).
  forest-combiner: review-6 architecture debt #1, the multi-forest
    prerequisite. Promote the BCF glue out of Chain (bcf_ pointer,
    drawGlue, combinedFits, formForestResponse, forestMultiplier,
    the if(bcf_) sweep branches) into a polymorphic ForestCombiner
    on the ResponseModel side owning per-forest residual formation,
    the coupling draw, combined fits, and per-forest reporting
    addressing; BCF becomes its first instance. Unblocks
    multinomial/heteroscedastic/hurdle AND grouped-x-multi-forest
    composition (GroupedResponse is on the wrong side of the
    Chain/combiner boundary today). RNG-neutral refactor, gated by
    the equivalence anchor + bcf-exact. Medium-large; land BEFORE
    any multi-forest model.
  forest-ranef-interweaving: research item filed 2026-07-11 from the
    tau slice review (docs/plans/tau-slice-review.md; VD approved
    filing). The measured grouped-fit mixing bottleneck is
    forest-ranef confounding (25x the tau IACT at K=3, weak signal;
    removing the forest recovers the isolation-experiment IACT), NOT
    the tau draw. Candidate remedies ranked by the review: (1) a
    joint or interweaving move between the forest fit and the
    random intercepts (the real lever; design from scratch); (2)
    ASIS on (tau, b) per the bcf-ridge-interweaving precedent -
    validated ~11x on the tau-b funnel in isolation but only
    PARTIAL in the full engine, so prototype-gate before committing.
    The tau-cauchy-exact-ig draw is a building block for (2).
    Research: needs a measurement harness (grouped SBC or IACT
    grid) before any engine work. decision-gated.
  gp-followups: sampled lengthscales (theta prior, per-sample channels,
    real cost - not the mechanical follow-up the proposal suggested);
    low-rank kernels. decision/consumer-gated.
  group-by-exposure: public group.by beyond rbart_vi
    (grouped-random-effects.md; naming reserved). decision-gated.
  grouped-equivalence: equivalence scenario for grouped rbart_vi fits,
    only if a grouped refactor is planned.
  grow-from-root: warm-start producer LANDED 2026-07-10 (c8c7764,
    grow-from-root-warm-start.md). Frontier 3.1's exact
    informed-proposal use of the shared scan remains open.
  interaction-constraints: structured sparsity and interaction limits
    on the SplitSelector seam. consumer-gated.
  monotone-bart: shape-constrained fits via the tree-level leaf-draw
    hook the design provisioned.
  multi-forest-models: multinomial, heteroscedastic, hurdle - the BCF
    two-forest machinery (forest-split-bcf, complete at c9fd2fe) is
    the template; one design note each when picked. Review-6
    prerequisites: forest-combiner FIRST (all three bend on it);
    heteroscedastic additionally needs a fourth leaf kind
    (multiplicative-positive, non-integrable) plus the non-conjugate
    MoveStrategy the design anticipated but never built, and a
    decision on per-observation residual variance (fold into the
    workingWeights channel vs a sigma vector).
  mutation-journal: build-new-and-swap for setPredictor instead of
    copy-old-and-restore; cell-granular journal for the patch paths;
    document the cost contract per entry point.
  negative-binomial: count outcomes via the Polya-Gamma NB
    augmentation (the PG sampler already ships); the r update decides
    integer vs real shape - a caveat shared with weighted-binary.
  ordinal-outcomes: cumulative probit on the existing truncated-normal
    machinery plus a cutpoint block.
  python-bindings: post kernel-cleanups the engine is R-free below the
    bridge; a pybind11 facade wrapper becomes prototype-scale. horizon,
    likely out-of-repo. decision-gated.
  repo-modernization: standing hygiene bundle. Remaining: PR-gate the
    sanitizers workflow once the new gcc-asan/valgrind legs prove
    stable on pushes; optional codecov badge (VD's call); optional
    roxygen2 and NEWS.md migrations (do not start unasked).
  robust-errors: Student-t residuals as a scale-mixture on the
    workingWeights hook; composes with user weights.
  sparse-extensions: in-place mutation, sparse x.test, streaming range
    kernel, mutation on dense-backed mixed columns (sparse-columns.md
    landing notes). The u8 width entry moved to data-ownership.
    consumer-gated.
  survival-models: AFT log-normal LANDED (f0efc03; design
    docs/design/survival.md; survival-grouped-surface reachable through
    rbart_vi landed as ac6ec2c). Remaining: discrete-time hazard
    (person-period ingestion over the binary families, same design note).
  warm-starts: v1 LANDED (installTrees + bart2 warm.start; same-grid
    v1, cross-grid refused). Remaining stretch: the cross-grid remap
    over mapOldCutPointsOntoNew; reopen when a consumer needs new-data
    warm starts.
  weighted-binary: PPD fix LANDED 2026-07-10 (da7b659) and issue #79
    closed. FUTURE (post 1.0): integer-weight probit via replicated
    latents; arbitrary real weights need a real-shape PG sampler (IPW
    is a pseudo-likelihood trap).
  within-chain-threading: previously assessed-and-deferred pending
    n >= 1e5 workloads, now confirmed common. Deterministic fixed-block
    reductions preserve thread-count invariance; the measurement
    interacts with data-ownership (same DRAM-bound regime) and competes
    with blocked-jacobi-trees as the mechanism.
  x86-simd: three linalg SSE2/AVX bodies are scalar with intrinsics
    commented out (predates the rewrite; the originals used
    non-temporal stores autovectorization cannot emit) - measure on
    x86, restore or delete; add misc_setIndexedVectorToConstant to the
    dispatch table; SSR SIMD leaf; Windows-arm64 NEON config.

